<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' 10-mth trade deficit at $10.090 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippines' 10-mth trade deficit at $10.090 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' trade deficit rose to $10.090 billion in the first ten months of the year, up from $7.148 billion in the same period last year, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit in October also rose to $944 million from the $740 million deficit recorded in October 1995, the office said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan-Oct 96   Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Oct 95</p>
<p>    Imports		  26,900	 24,059	  21,552</p>
<p>    Exports		  16,810	 14,926	  14,404</p>
<p>    Trade Deficit	  10,090	  9,132	   7,148</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE     Oct 96	Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p>    Imports		   2,827	 2,853	   2,342</p>
<p>    Exports		   1,884	 1,876	   1,602</p>
<p>    Trade Deficit	     944	   977	     740</p>
<p>Note: Figures in million U.S. dollars. Components may not add up to total due to rounding off of figures.</p>
</text>
